---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting Started"
  description="Install Puerto and scaffold your first Rust DDD project in under a minute."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen pt-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[240px_1fr] lg:gap-12">

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      <aside class="hidden lg:block">
        <nav class="sticky top-28 space-y-1" aria-label="Documentation navigation">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-puerto-mist/50">Getting Started</p>
          <a href="#installation" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Installation</a>
          <a href="#new-project" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">New Project</a>
          <a href="#scaffold" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Generate Scaffold</a>
          <a href="#entity-fields" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Entity Fields</a>
          <a href="#value-objects" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Value Objects</a>
          <a href="#layer-generators" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Layer Generators</a>
          <a href="#web" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Web Frontend</a>
          <a href="#use-case" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Add Use Case</a>
          <a href="#database" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Database (SQLx)</a>
          <a href="#events" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Domain events</a>
          <a href="#architecture" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Architecture</a>
          <a href="#runtime" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Runtime crates</a>
          <a href="#production" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">Production defaults</a>
          <a href="#ai-agents" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">AI agents</a>
          <a href="#cli" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">CLI reference</a>
          <a href="#snippets" class="doc-link block rounded px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist transition-colors hover:bg-puerto-navy hover:text-puerto-ice">IDE Snippets</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <!-- Content -->
      <article class="prose-puerto min-w-0">
        <h1 class="font-mono text-4xl font-bold text-puerto-ice lg:text-5xl">Getting Started</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-lg text-puerto-mist">
          Puerto is a CLI tool that scaffolds production-ready Rust backends with Domain-Driven Design architecture. From install to running API in under a minute.
        </p>

        <!-- Prerequisites -->
        <div class="mt-8 rounded-md border border-puerto-teal/30 bg-puerto-teal/5 px-5 py-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-teal">Prerequisites</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>Rust stable (1.85+) — <a href="https://rustup.rs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-puerto-teal hover:underline">install via rustup</a></li>
            <li>Cargo (included with Rust)</li>
            <li>Optional: Docker + <a href="https://github.com/launchbadge/sqlx/tree/main/sqlx-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-puerto-teal hover:underline">SQLx CLI</a> for database projects — <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">docker-compose.yml</code> runs Postgres, the CLI runs migrations and the query cache</li>
            <li>Optional: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">cmake</code> and the libcurl headers for <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">--events kafka</code> projects (librdkafka is built from source)</li>
            <li>Optional: <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-puerto-teal hover:underline">Bun</a> for the web frontend (skip it with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">--no-web</code>)</li>
            <li>Generated projects pin their toolchain (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">rust-toolchain.toml</code>, Rust 1.95.0) — rustup installs it on the first build</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Installation -->
        <section id="installation" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Installation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">Install the Puerto CLI from crates.io:</p>
          <div class="code-block mt-4 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">cargo install puerto --locked</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="cargo install puerto --locked" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">Verify the installation:</p>
          <div class="code-block mt-2 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto --version</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- New Project -->
        <section id="new-project" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">New Project</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Create a new Puerto workspace. The interactive wizard asks for your project name, whether you need database support, whether to include the Greeting demo entity, and whether to include the web frontend.
          </p>
          <div class="code-block mt-4 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto new</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto new" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">For non-interactive use (CI/scripts):</p>
          <div class="code-block mt-2 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto new --name my-app --db --no-demo</code>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Generated structure:</p>
          <div class="mt-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy p-5 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <div class="text-puerto-mist/60">my-app/</div>
            <div class="pl-4"><span class="text-puerto-teal">business/</span><span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← domain + application</span></div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/domain/greeting/</div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/application/greeting/</div>
            <div class="pl-4 mt-1"><span class="text-puerto-indigo">infrastructure/</span><span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← adapters</span></div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/greeting/repository.rs</div>
            <div class="pl-4 mt-1"><span class="text-puerto-rust">presentation/</span><span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← http api</span></div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/api/greeting/routes.rs</div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/main.rs<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← hands the server to puerto-web</span></div>
            <div class="pl-8 text-puerto-mist/50">src/app.rs<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← your middleware + routes, never regenerated</span></div>
            <div class="pl-4 mt-1"><span class="text-puerto-teal">web/</span><span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← React + daisyUI on Bun (--no-web skips it)</span></div>
            <div class="pl-4 mt-1 text-puerto-mist/50">puerto.toml<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← source of truth</span></div>
            <div class="pl-4 text-puerto-mist/50">AGENTS.md + CLAUDE.md<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← rules for coding agents</span></div>
            <div class="pl-4 text-puerto-mist/50">rust-toolchain.toml<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← pinned Rust, reproducible lint</span></div>
            <div class="pl-4 text-puerto-mist/50">Cargo.toml<span class="text-puerto-mist/40 ml-3">← edition 2024 workspace + Puerto runtime crates</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Scaffold -->
        <section id="scaffold" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Generate Scaffold</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Scaffold a complete DDD entity across all layers. Puerto creates the domain model, repository trait, use cases, infrastructure adapter, and presentation routes — wired together automatically.
          </p>
          <div class="code-block mt-4 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold User</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate scaffold User" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">What gets created:</p>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono">business/</span><span>model.rs, errors.rs, repository.rs (trait + mockall mock), 5 use cases (create, get, list, update, delete), each trait with its mock</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-indigo font-mono">infrastructure/</span><span>repository (InMemory or Pg — inferred from puerto.toml)</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-rust font-mono">presentation/</span><span>routes.rs (holds use case ports, tested per status with mocked use cases), dto.rs, responses.rs, error_mapper.rs</span></div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Running it twice:</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Scaffolding an entity that already exists is <span class="font-semibold text-puerto-ice">refused</span> — those ~15 files are yours once written, and overwriting them silently would discard any business rule, custom use case body or test you added. In a terminal Puerto lists the files and asks; in CI it aborts without writing a byte.
          </p>
          <div class="code-block mt-3 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-rust bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold User --force</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate scaffold User --force" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">--force</code> overwrites them and updates the <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">[[entity]]</code> block in place, so the manifest keeps describing the code on disk. Use cases you added with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">puerto generate use-case</code> survive; edits inside the regenerated files do not.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Entity Fields -->
        <section id="entity-fields" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Entity Fields</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Define typed fields on your entities. The type system flows through every DDD layer — domain model, Params, DTOs, repository rows, and SQL migrations all derive from the field list.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-5 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">From the CLI:</p>
          <div class="mt-2 code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold Product -- name:String price:i64! sku:String</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate scaffold Product -- name:String price:i64! sku:String" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Fields go after <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">--</code> (required separator). Append <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">!</code> after a type to mark it as unique (e.g., <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">sku:String!</code> generates a unique DB constraint). Fields are persisted to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code> and used by all generators.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Or edit puerto.toml directly:</p>
          <div class="mt-2 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy p-5 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <div class="text-puerto-mist/60">[[entity]]</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">name = "Product"</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">use_cases = ["create_product", "list_products"]</div>
            <div class="mt-2 text-puerto-mist/60">[[entity.fields]]</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">name = "name"</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">type = "String"</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-puerto-mist/60">[[entity.fields]]</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">name = "price"</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">type = "i64"</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-puerto-mist/60">[[entity.fields]]</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">name = "sku"</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-ice">type = "String"</div>
            <div class="text-puerto-teal">unique = true</div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Supported types:</p>
          <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/30">
                  <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist/60 uppercase tracking-wider">Rust Type</th>
                  <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist/60 uppercase tracking-wider">SQL Type</th>
                  <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist/60 uppercase tracking-wider">OpenAPI</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="font-sans text-puerto-mist">
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">String</td><td class="pr-4">TEXT</td><td>string</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">i64</td><td class="pr-4">BIGINT</td><td>integer(int64)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">bool</td><td class="pr-4">BOOLEAN</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">f64</td><td class="pr-4">DOUBLE</td><td>number(double)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">Uuid</td><td class="pr-4">UUID</td><td>string(uuid)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">DateTime&lt;Utc&gt;</td><td class="pr-4">TIMESTAMPTZ</td><td>string(date-time)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">Option&lt;T&gt;</td><td class="pr-4">nullable</td><td>T?</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">Vec&lt;String&gt;</td><td class="pr-4">TEXT[]</td><td>array[string]</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-4 font-mono text-puerto-ice">HashMap&lt;String, String&gt;</td><td class="pr-4">JSONB</td><td>object</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Every entity always includes <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">id</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">created_at</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">updated_at</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">deleted</code>, and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">deleted_at</code> as system fields — these are generated automatically and should not be added to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code>.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            If <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">entity.fields</code> is empty or absent, entities default to a single <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">name: String</code> field for backward compatibility.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Validate your configuration:</p>
          <div class="mt-2 code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto validate</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto validate" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Checks entity names (PascalCase), field names (snake_case), field types (against the type registry), duplicate entities and fields, reserved names (Rust keywords, SQL reserved words in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">--db</code> projects), and that every declared entity has its code on disk. In events projects it also checks custom events and consumers. It warns about <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">Option&lt;T&gt;</code> fields marked <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">unique</code> and about runtime crates on another minor than the CLI.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Value Objects -->
        <section id="value-objects" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Value Objects</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Wrap primitive fields in strongly-typed Value Objects. Puerto generates the VO structs, error variants, and all layer conversions automatically — domain, application, infrastructure, and presentation.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Field syntax</p>
          <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/30">
                  <th class="py-2 pr-6 text-left font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist/60 uppercase tracking-wider">Format</th>
                  <th class="py-2 text-left font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist/60 uppercase tracking-wider">Result</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="font-sans text-puerto-mist">
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">name:Name:String</td><td class="text-xs">String VO wrapping a primitive</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">age:Age:i64</td><td class="text-xs">Numeric VO (i64 / f64), pass-through</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">mid:Mid:opt:String</td><td class="text-xs"><code class="text-puerto-teal">Option&lt;Mid&gt;</code> — nullable VO</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">tags:Tag:vec:String</td><td class="text-xs"><code class="text-puerto-teal">Vec&lt;Tag&gt;</code> — array VO</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">status:Status:enum:A/B/C</td><td class="text-xs">Enum VO — <code class="text-puerto-teal">FromStr</code> (<code class="text-puerto-teal">.parse::&lt;Status&gt;()</code>) / <code class="text-puerto-teal">as_str()</code></td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">sku:Sku:String!</td><td class="text-xs">Unique VO (DB constraint)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="py-1.5 pr-6 font-mono text-puerto-ice text-xs">email:Email</td><td class="text-xs">Shared VO — type inferred from <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Example</p>
          <div class="mt-2 code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold Order -- amount:Amount:f64 status:Status:enum:Pending/Confirmed/Cancelled</code>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">What gets generated</p>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono flex-none">domain/</span><span><code class="font-mono text-xs">value_objects.rs</code> with VO structs, <code class="font-mono text-xs">Invalid*</code> error variants, model using VO types</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono flex-none">application/</span><span>params use primitives; use case impl constructs VOs before calling <code class="font-mono text-xs">Entity::new()</code></span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-indigo font-mono flex-none">infrastructure/</span><span>DB row uses primitives; <code class="font-mono text-xs">TryFrom</code> reconstructs VOs, <code class="font-mono text-xs">From</code> extracts them</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-rust font-mono flex-none">presentation/</span><span>DTO uses primitives; <code class="font-mono text-xs">from_domain()</code> calls <code class="font-mono text-xs">.value()</code> / <code class="font-mono text-xs">.as_str()</code></span></div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Shared Value Objects</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">Declare reusable VOs once — any entity can reference them by name and the type is inferred automatically:</p>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-2">
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate value-object Email String</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate value-object Email String" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold User -- email:Email name:Name:String</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate scaffold User -- email:Email name:Name:String" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Shared VOs are declared in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code> as <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">[[value_object]]</code> entries and generated at <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">business/src/domain/shared/value_objects.rs</code>. Their import path switches to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">crate::domain::shared::value_objects</code> automatically.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">Validation</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">puerto validate</code> checks VO names (PascalCase), inner types (allowed primitives), enum variants (PascalCase, non-empty), and rejects <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">unique</code> on <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">Option&lt;T&gt;</code> or <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">Vec&lt;T&gt;</code> VOs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Layer Generators -->
        <section id="layer-generators" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Layer Generators</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Generate one DDD layer at a time. Ideal for AI-assisted development — keeping each agent focused on a single layer prevents context drift and makes compiler errors immediately actionable.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-3">
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate domain Product</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate domain Product" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate application Product</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate application Product" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-indigo bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate repository Product</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate repository Product" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-rust bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate presentation Product</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate presentation Product" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono flex-none">domain</span><span>model, errors, repository trait, 5 use case traits, <span class="text-puerto-indigo font-mono">ProductMother</span> (Object Mother) — registers entity in puerto.toml</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono flex-none">application</span><span>5 use case implementations with unit tests</span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-indigo font-mono flex-none">repository</span><span>InMemory or Pg adapter — inferred from <span class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</span></span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-rust font-mono flex-none">presentation</span><span>routes with route tests, dto, responses, error mapper — regenerates <span class="font-mono text-xs">bootstrap.rs</span></span></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-puerto-teal font-mono flex-none">web</span><span>web projects: the entity's screens — see <a href="#web" class="text-puerto-teal hover:underline">Web Frontend</a></span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-5 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Each command validates the prior step completed and prints a <span class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">Next:</span> hint. Use <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold</code> when you want all layers at once.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Web frontend -->
        <section id="web" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Web Frontend</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Every project includes <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">web/</code> unless created with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">--no-web</code>: React 19 + daisyUI 5 on Bun, routed with wouter, typed from the API's OpenAPI spec. It follows the same Dependency Rule as the crates — <span class="font-mono text-xs">domain</span>, <span class="font-mono text-xs">infrastructure</span> (HTTP adapter), <span class="font-mono text-xs">presentation</span> — checked by dependency-cruiser.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold</code> writes a CRUD entity's screens next to its Rust layers: list, detail and a create/edit form, an HTTP repository over openapi-fetch, an Object Mother and an in-memory fake, all with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">bun test</code> tests. Every field type gets its input — text, number, checkbox, <span class="font-mono text-xs">datetime-local</span>, a <span class="font-mono text-xs">select</span> for enums, empty-means-<span class="font-mono text-xs">null</span> for optionals. A rejected form says what went wrong next to the field: <span class="font-mono text-xs">messages.ts</span>, generated from the same codes as <span class="font-mono text-xs">errors.rs</span>, maps each code to a message and a field; list pages live in the URL (<span class="font-mono text-xs">?page=2</span>). Your own screens go in <span class="font-mono text-xs">core/routes.tsx</span>, which no generator touches. The route table and the composition root are regenerated from <span class="font-mono text-xs">puerto.toml</span>, like <span class="font-mono text-xs">bootstrap.rs</span>.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-3">
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">make web/sync</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="make web/sync" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">make web/install &amp;&amp; make web/dev</code>
              <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="make web/install && make web/dev" aria-label="Copy">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-1 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>• <span class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">make web/sync</span> after a scaffold or a DTO change: a Rust test exports <span class="font-mono text-xs">docs/api/openapi.json</span> and the frontend's wire types are regenerated from it. Until then <span class="font-mono text-xs">bun run typecheck</span> fails — that is the drift check.</li>
            <li>• <span class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">puerto generate web Product</span> writes the screens alone, for an entity already in <span class="font-mono text-xs">puerto.toml</span> — the last step of the layer-by-layer flow.</li>
            <li>• No client-side copy of domain validation: the form shows the code the API answers (<span class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">product.validation_error.name_empty</span>).</li>
            <li>• The dev server proxies <span class="font-mono text-xs">/api</span> to <span class="font-mono text-xs">:8080</span>: no CORS in development.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Use Case -->
        <section id="use-case" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Add a Use Case</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Add a use case to an existing entity. Puerto generates the trait and implementation, declares them in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">lib.rs</code>, adds the use case to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">UserApi</code> and rewires <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">bootstrap.rs</code> — the project keeps compiling. Expose it by adding an endpoint to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">routes.rs</code>.
          </p>
          <div class="code-block mt-4 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-teal bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate use-case User archive_user</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="puerto generate use-case User archive_user" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Database -->
        <section id="database" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Database (SQLx)</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Puerto has first-class SQLx + Postgres support. Enable it when creating a project — Puerto infers the choice for every subsequent scaffold automatically.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-indigo bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto new --name my-app --db</code>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-indigo bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate scaffold User</code>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate migration create_users_table</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Puerto reads <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code> to decide: db projects get a <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">PgUserRepository</code> with a connection pool and auto-created migration; non-db projects get <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">InMemoryUserRepository</code>. No flag needed on every scaffold.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">After a scaffold:</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Queries are checked at compile time against an offline cache (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">.sqlx/</code>, commit it). A new entity's queries are not in it yet, so the build asks for it until you apply the migration and refresh the cache. Both targets start Postgres from <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">docker-compose.yml</code>:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-indigo bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">make sqlx/migrate &amp;&amp; make sqlx/prepare</code>
            <button class="copy-btn ml-auto cursor-pointer text-puerto-mist hover:text-puerto-ice" data-copy="make sqlx/migrate && make sqlx/prepare" aria-label="Copy">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Migrations also run at startup, and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">make run</code> starts the database first. <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">make test/infrastructure</code> runs the repositories' <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">#[sqlx::test]</code>s, each against a throwaway database.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>• Every scaffold writes its own migration; versions stay unique even when two entities are scaffolded within the same second.</li>
            <li>• Driver errors are mapped in one place, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">map_sqlx_error</code> from the <a href="#runtime" class="text-puerto-teal hover:underline">puerto-sqlx</a> runtime crate: a unique violation (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">23505</code>) becomes <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">409</code>, with an integration test per <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">unique</code> field.</li>
            <li>• Deletes are soft, so <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">unique</code> fields get a partial index (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">WHERE deleted = false</code>): a deleted row never keeps its value taken.</li>
            <li>• Field names that are SQL reserved words (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">order</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">user</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">desc</code>…) are rejected up front instead of breaking the migration.</li>
            <li>• <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto generate migration</code> is only available in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">--db</code> projects.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Domain events -->
        <section id="events" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Domain events</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            A <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">--db</code> project can record an event with every write: the entity and its event are saved in one transaction, in an <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">outbox</code> table, so an event is never lost and never sent for a write that rolled back. A second process, the worker, relays the outbox and runs your consumers.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 border-l-4 border-l-puerto-indigo bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto new --name shop --db --events db</code>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate event Product product_published</code>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">puerto generate consumer notify_new_product --on product_created,product_published</code>
            </div>
            <div class="code-block flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy px-5 py-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-teal select-none">$</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-puerto-ice">make worker</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>• Each CRUD entity gets a generated <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">events.rs</code> (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">ProductEvent::Created(ProductSnapshot)</code>, …) and a unit of work. Its repository only reads, so a write that skips the outbox does not compile.</li>
            <li>• The CRUD use cases record created / updated / deleted for you. A custom event is recorded by your use case, in the same unit of work as the write: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">uow.save(&amp;product)</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">uow.record(ProductEvent::Published(ProductSnapshot::from_entity(&amp;product)))</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">uow.commit()</code>. Return early with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">?</code> and both roll back.</li>
            <li>• A consumer is an <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">EventHandler</code> that answers <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">Ack</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">Retry</code> (redelivered with a 1 s → 300 s backoff) or a dead letter. Nothing is dropped without a row in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">dead_letters</code> (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">make events/dead-letters</code>). Delivery is at-least-once: handlers are idempotent.</li>
            <li>• <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">--events db</code> needs no broker: deliveries are rows in Postgres. <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">--events kafka</code> publishes each event to its aggregate's topic, keyed by the aggregate id, so one aggregate's events are consumed in order; each consumer is a consumer group, and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">docker-compose.yml</code> runs Redpanda for development. It builds librdkafka from source: install <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">cmake</code> and the libcurl headers (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">libcurl4-openssl-dev</code> on Debian/Ubuntu).</li>
            <li>• The worker serves <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">/health</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">/health/ready</code> on <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-mist">WORKER_PORT</code> (8081) and drains on SIGTERM, like the API.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Architecture -->
        <section id="architecture" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Architecture</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Puerto enforces a strict dependency rule: dependencies only point inward. The domain layer has zero external dependencies.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-puerto-steel/40 bg-puerto-navy p-6 font-mono text-sm">
            <div class="text-puerto-mist/50 text-xs mb-4">dependency flow (inward only)</div>
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="w-36 text-puerto-rust">presentation/</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-mist/40">→ depends on</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-indigo">infrastructure/</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="w-36 text-puerto-indigo">infrastructure/</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-mist/40">→ depends on</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-teal">business/</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="w-36 text-puerto-teal">business/</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-mist/40">→ depends on</span>
                <span class="text-puerto-mist/60">no other crate of the workspace</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            Modules are declared inline in each crate's <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">lib.rs</code> — no <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">mod.rs</code> files. Logging goes through <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">tracing</code> directly: no logger to inject or mock.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">Typed ids</span> — every entity's id is its own type (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">UserId</code>), so passing another entity's id is a compile error. It is a plain UUID on the wire and in the database.</li>
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">One repository error</span> — every repository port returns <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">RepositoryError</code> (<span class="font-mono text-xs">Duplicate</span>, <span class="font-mono text-xs">InvalidData</span>, <span class="font-mono text-xs">Unavailable</span>); each entity's error converts it, so use cases just use <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">?</code>.</li>
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">Paged lists</span> — <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">PageRequest</code> caps the page size in the domain: no route, use case or adapter can read an unbounded table.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Runtime crates -->
        <section id="runtime" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Runtime crates</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Puerto generates what is yours — entities, use cases, repositories, routes, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">bootstrap.rs</code>. What is identical in every project and not meant to be edited is not copied in: it is a crate, declared once in the root <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">Cargo.toml</code> on the same minor as the <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto</code> CLI. A fix to the server or the Postgres error mapping reaches your project with <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">cargo update</code>.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/30 text-left text-xs text-puerto-mist/60">
                  <th class="py-2 pr-6 font-normal">Crate</th><th class="py-2 pr-6 font-normal">Owns</th><th class="py-2 font-normal">Used by</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">puerto-core</td><td class="py-2 pr-6 text-xs"><code class="text-puerto-ice">RepositoryError</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">PageRequest</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">Page&lt;T&gt;</code>; the event envelope, <code class="text-puerto-ice">EventHandler</code> and the transport ports — no I/O, no runtime</td><td class="py-2 font-mono text-xs">business</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto-web</td><td class="py-2 pr-6 text-xs">the server (tracing, CORS, graceful shutdown), <code class="text-puerto-ice">Config::from_env</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">/health</code> + <code class="text-puerto-ice">/health/ready</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">ErrorResponse</code></td><td class="py-2 font-mono text-xs">presentation</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-indigo-light">puerto-sqlx</td><td class="py-2 pr-6 text-xs">the Postgres pool, migrations at startup, the readiness ping, <code class="text-puerto-ice">map_sqlx_error</code>; with events, the unit of work, the outbox and the <code class="text-puerto-ice">db</code> transport</td><td class="py-2 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs">infrastructure (<span class="text-puerto-teal">--db</span>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">puerto-events</td><td class="py-2 pr-6 text-xs">the worker: the outbox relay, the consume loops and their delivery policy, health probes, graceful shutdown</td><td class="py-2 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs">worker (<span class="text-puerto-teal">--events</span>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto-kafka</td><td class="py-2 pr-6 text-xs">the Kafka transport: <code class="text-puerto-ice">KafkaPublisher</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">KafkaSubscription</code></td><td class="py-2 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs">worker (<span class="text-puerto-teal">--events kafka</span>)</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            The runtime is a library, not a host: your <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">main.rs</code> calls <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">App::new(config).try_serve(build_app)</code>, and the generated <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">bootstrap.rs</code> stays plain, readable Rust. Extra middleware and routes go in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">presentation/src/app.rs</code>, which no generator touches. A startup failure is a message, not a panic: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">build_app</code> returns <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">Result&lt;_, String&gt;</code> with a hint (<span class="font-mono text-xs">.env</span>, <span class="font-mono text-xs">make docker-compose/up</span>), the error says <span class="font-mono text-xs">host:port/database</span> but never the password, and the process exits 1. <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">puerto validate</code> warns when the runtime and the CLI drift apart.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Production defaults -->
        <section id="production" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">Production defaults</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Every generated project ships with what a service needs before its first deploy — and passes its own <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">make lint</code> (clippy <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">-D warnings</code>) out of the box.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">GET /health</td><td class="text-xs">Liveness — the process answers</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">GET /health/ready</td><td class="text-xs">Readiness — <code class="text-puerto-teal">503</code> until the database answers (<code class="text-puerto-teal">--db</code> projects)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">SIGTERM / Ctrl-C</td><td class="text-xs">Graceful shutdown — in-flight requests drain before exit</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">Error bodies</td><td class="text-xs"><code class="text-puerto-teal">&#123;"name": "user.not_found", …&#125;</code> — a machine-readable code clients can branch on</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">Status codes</td><td class="text-xs">Validation <code class="text-puerto-teal">422</code> · not found <code class="text-puerto-teal">404</code> · duplicate <code class="text-puerto-teal">409</code> · storage <code class="text-puerto-teal">500</code> — one generated test per mapping</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">GET /users?limit=&amp;offset=</td><td class="text-xs">Paged lists — <code class="text-puerto-teal">&#123;"items", "total", "limit", "offset"&#125;</code>, 20 per page by default, capped at 100 by the domain</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">rust-toolchain.toml</td><td class="text-xs">Pinned Rust: the lint gives the same answer on every machine</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- AI agents -->
        <section id="ai-agents" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">AI agents</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Every project ships instructions for coding agents: a root <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">AGENTS.md</code> (architecture, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto</code> commands, conventions, the checks to run) imported by <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">CLAUDE.md</code>, plus one per crate. Puerto's own test suite keeps them in sync with what it generates.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">One commit per piece</span> — finish a use case, get tests and lint green, commit, move on.</li>
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">Risk tiers</span> — migrations, money, auth and uniqueness rules get a human read of the full diff; DTO mapping and docs trust the checks.</li>
            <li>• <span class="text-puerto-ice">Decisions written down</span> — design choices go to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">docs/adr/</code>, so the next session inherits the reason.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- CLI reference -->
        <section id="cli" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-puerto-ice">CLI reference</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-puerto-mist">
            Every command runs from the project root and reads <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-rust">puerto.toml</code>. Generators refuse to overwrite files you own unless told to, and a command that does not apply to the project (a migration without <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">--db</code>, a consumer without <code class="font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">--events</code>) says so instead of writing anything.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/30 text-left text-xs text-puerto-mist/60">
                  <th class="py-2 pr-6 font-normal">Command</th><th class="py-2 font-normal">What it does</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">puerto new</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">New workspace — <code class="text-puerto-ice">--name</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--db</code> / <code class="text-puerto-ice">--no-db</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--events db|kafka</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--no-demo</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--no-web</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--destination</code></td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate scaffold &lt;Name&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Every layer of an entity, its screens and its migration — fields after <code class="text-puerto-ice">--</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">--force</code> to overwrite</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate &lt;layer&gt; &lt;Name&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">One layer at a time: <code class="text-puerto-ice">domain</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">application</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">repository</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">presentation</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">web</code> (which takes <code class="text-puerto-ice">--force</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate use-case &lt;Entity&gt; &lt;action&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">A use case trait, its implementation and its mock, wired into the entity's API</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate value-object &lt;Name&gt; &lt;type&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">A shared value object any entity can use by name</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate migration &lt;name&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">An empty SQLx migration (<code class="text-puerto-ice">--db</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate event &lt;Entity&gt; &lt;name&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">A custom domain event; regenerates <code class="text-puerto-ice">events.rs</code> (<code class="text-puerto-ice">--events</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate consumer &lt;name&gt; --on a,b</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">A worker consumer with its tests; regenerates the registry (<code class="text-puerto-ice">--events</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate bootstrap</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Rewrites <code class="text-puerto-ice">bootstrap.rs</code> and the web composition root; refuses while a declared entity has no code (<code class="text-puerto-ice">--allow-missing</code> writes it anyway)</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">generate snippets</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Rewrites the IDE snippet files — <code class="text-puerto-ice">--ide zed|vscode</code></td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">list</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Entities, their adapter, use cases and events; shared value objects; consumers</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">validate</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Checks <code class="text-puerto-ice">puerto.toml</code> against the rules and the code on disk</td></tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-teal">completions &lt;shell&gt;</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">Shell completion script — <code class="text-puerto-ice">bash</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">zsh</code>, <code class="text-puerto-ice">fish</code>, …</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-puerto-ice">In the generated project</p>
          <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full font-sans text-sm text-puerto-mist">
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-puerto-steel/10"><td class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-puerto-ice">make run · make worker</td><td class="py-2 text-xs">The API on <code class="text-puerto-teal">:8080</code> (Swagger UI at <code class="text-puerto-teal">/</code>, endpoints under <code class="text-puerto-teal">/api</code>) · the worker on <code class="text-puerto-teal">:8081</code></td></tr>
